message: "If you use librarian in your research or workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "librarian: A Local-First, Plain-Text Activity Tracker with Pluggable Schemas and an MCP Server"
abstract: >
  librarian is a CRUD and search tool over a YAML database of activity entries.
  Each entry has fixed core fields (id, date, title, description, tags,
  supporting docs) plus optional structured blocks defined by a pluggable
  schema. It ships as a command-line tool, an MCP server enabling AI
  assistants to read and update the database, and ready-made schemas for
  common reporting workflows (post-tenure review, continuing-education
  credits, scholarly portfolios). The goal is to turn periodic reporting
  cycles (annual reviews, post-tenure review, certification renewal,
  retrospective documentation) into a query against a maintained record
  instead of a memory exercise.
